    "Description": "A transparency slide that shows a detail of the right front quarter and saddle of a carousel pig that is very worn. The skin of the pig is a light tan, but gets darker towards the top, almost to black. The tack is red with a brown clasp. The saddle is brown. The saddle blanket is green. The saddle strap is blue. There are many spots where the paint has worn away. Where the front leg meets the body there is a crack visible along with some minor loss. The pig is suspended on a pole. The slide reads “PULLEN PARK CAROUSEL PULLEN PARK 16B” at the top and “RALEIGH NC WAKE CO S.S. 8.5.81 JUL81D9” at the bottom.",
